%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ce052722ed547544eb4bbaf99ed6d422, type: 3}
  m_Name: StepperTool
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  ToolName: start_import_step
  ToolDescription: |-
    Starts importing from the given step index and continues automatically until completion or until a user action is required.
    The optional sprite_duplicate_resolution only resolves an already pending SpriteDuplicateRemover pause after the user explicitly chooses default duplicate handling or keeping all duplicates. It does not preconfigure future import steps.
    The response is JSON with status, message, next_step, requires_user_action, pause_reason, requires_explicit_user_choice, user_message, agent_instruction, and available_actions.
  InstanceTypeName: DA_Assets.FCU.FigmaConverterUnity
  InstanceLabel: FCU
  Schema:
    Type: object
    Properties:
      m_Keys:
      - step_index
      - sprite_duplicate_resolution
      m_Values:
      - Type: integer
        Description: Import step index to execute (0-based). Use 0 to initialize
          the import.
      - Type: string
        Description: Optional duplicate handling for an already pending SpriteDuplicateRemover
          pause. Only pass this after interpreting the user's explicit natural-language
          choice. Internally use apply_default to apply the default selected duplicates
          or keep_all_duplicates to deselect all duplicates and continue. Do not show
          these internal values to the user. If the user handles duplicates manually
          in Unity, omit this argument when continuing with the returned next_step.
    Required:
    - step_index
  ResponseTemplates:
    m_Keys:
    - sprite_duplicate_user_message
    - sprite_duplicate_agent_instruction
    m_Values:
    - How would you like to handle duplicate sprites? I can apply the default duplicate selection, keep all duplicates, or you can choose the sprites manually in Unity and then tell me to continue the import.
    - Show user_message to the user in their language. Do not show internal action names, JSON field names, or a command list. Interpret the user's reply: default duplicate selection => call next_step with sprite_duplicate_resolution=apply_default; keep all duplicates => call next_step with sprite_duplicate_resolution=keep_all_duplicates; manual Unity selection => wait until the user says they are done, then call next_step without sprite_duplicate_resolution.
